From 513ba5e545a03e87aa6b900215d3394430205d6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:20:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 178/206] [vm] Shorebird: put Thread's Shorebird fields at
 Shorebird's offsets (F147)

Our 16 Shorebird Thread fields were appended after
regexp_backtracking_stack_cache_. Shorebird's sit in four blocks inside the
upstream layout. Every Thread offset after the first block therefore differed
from theirs, and every instruction or pool slot that encodes one differed too.

Move them to Shorebird's positions, in Shorebird's order (their Flutter.framework
dSYM, Thread byte_size 0xf78):
  after resume_interpreter_adjusted_entry_point_  resume_on_simulator_, resume_on_cpu_
      (0x288/0x290), as CACHED_VM_STUBS_ADDRESSES_LIST entries -- their
      InitVMConstants stores 0x280, 0x288, 0x290, 0x298 in one run
  after saved_shadow_call_stack_  base_instructions_entry_point_, _end_ (0x700/0x708)
  after random_  is_simulating_ .. exit_safepoint_entry_point_ (0x8d8..0x928), plus a
      never-used placeholder exit_safepoint_ignore_unwind_in_progress_entry_point_
      at 0x930 (its runtime entry was deleted upstream in 8085a97a637)
  after thread_locals_  indirect_static_call_table_ (0x978)

resume_on_*_entry_point_ are now written by InitVMConstants (INIT_VALUE), so the
explicit writes in SetupDartMutatorStateDependingOnSnapshot are removed, and
their *_offset() getters now come from DEFINE_OFFSET_METHOD.

The shift moves 218 Thread entries (+0x10/+0x20/+0x80) in the four arm64
non-compressed sections of runtime_offsets_extracted.h ({,!}PRODUCT x
{JIT,AOT}). Those sections were regenerated with offsets_extractor and
offsets_extractor_aotruntime built from this tree (ReleaseARM64, ProductARM64,
ProductSimARM64 configs; Sim == Product), and spliced in place: 0 differing
entries afterwards. No non-Thread entry changed.

NOT regenerated: the compressed-pointer and non-arm64 sections. The fields are
unconditional, so those configurations now fail CheckOffsets until
tools/run_offsets_extractor.dart is rerun for them. No local build uses them.

